WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.180
Two routes feed one axon.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.300
How can you tell which route makes which part of the firing?

3
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:12.103
Take one route away, and watch which phase is left.

4
00:00:13.023 --> 00:00:15.743
Here, the route taken away is always the Merkel cell's.

5
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:21.133
The recordings come from mouse skin, kept alive in a bath with its nerve attached.

6
00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:25.923
An electrode records one afferent while a probe presses the skin.

7
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:30.213
The recorded afferent lacks the light-activated proteins.

8
00:00:31.393 --> 00:00:35.393
Light aimed at the touch dome, plus controls, ties the effects to Merkel cells.

9
00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:42.297
First test. Light aimed at the Merkel cells depolarizes them, with no touch at all.

10
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.430
The afferent fires.

11
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.210
The Merkel cell is enough to drive it.

12
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.860
Second test. Light silences the Merkel cells during a held press.

13
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.760
What do you expect to lose?

14
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.623
The sustained firing is suppressed.

15
00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.603
The hold needs the Merkel cell in the moment.

16
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:12.217
Third test. Delete Piezo2 from the skin's epithelium, but not from the nerve.

17
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:18.737
In culture, Merkel cells without epithelial Piezo2 lose their touch-evoked current.

18
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:20.937
The ending keeps its channel.

19
00:01:21.837 --> 00:01:22.837
Predict what is left.

20
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.810
The onset stays similar to controls.

21
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.030
The hold loses its normal sustained firing.

22
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.050
That is the cleanest split.

23
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:42.850
One limit. This deletion covers all of the skin's epithelium, not only the Merkel

24
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:43.850
cells.

25
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:50.343
Fourth test. Remove the Merkel cells altogether, by deleting the gene Atoh1 during

26
00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.343
development.

27
00:01:51.916 --> 00:01:53.816
The afferents still respond to touch.

28
00:01:54.596 --> 00:01:57.036
But the hold is cut short, before the press ends.

29
00:01:57.856 --> 00:01:59.496
That is called intermediately adapting.

30
00:02:00.616 --> 00:02:02.116
And the onset falls too.

31
00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.116
Peak firing drops to about a third of normal.

32
00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:07.829
That row only partly fits.

33
00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:12.949
A developmental loss cannot say whether the cell's own signal, or a changed skin,

34
00:02:13.249 --> 00:02:14.249
caused it.

35
00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:19.843
Blocking vesicle release in the epidermis, with tetanus toxin, also reduced both

36
00:02:19.843 --> 00:02:20.843
phases.

37
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:25.363
So release, probably from Merkel cells, may help with the onset too.

38
00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.223
That is why the idea says mainly.

39
00:02:33.163 --> 00:02:37.823
In mouse touch domes, the ending mainly feels the change, and the Merkel cell mainly

40
00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:40.483
holds the press. Neither acts alone.
